tp://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135391913,imgsize-1714149.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NASA-funded study reveals 4.1-billion-year-old history of pink Martian rock found in Sahara]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135396990.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Discovered in the vast Sahara Desert, the meteorite Teghaza 001 is over four billion years old and is confirmed to be a Martian rock via isotopic studies. This intriguing specimen reveals a volcanic history intertwined with water activity, indicating a complex water cycle on Mars. As researchers delve deeper into its origins, they are unraveling vital insights into the planet's early environmental conditions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/in-2022-an-800-gram-pink-rock-was-found-in-the-sahara-desert-nasa-funded-researchers-have-now-confirmed-it-came-from-mars-more-than-4-1-billion-years-ago-and-preserves-signs-of-the-planets-ancient-water/articleshow/135396990.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/in-2022-an-800-gram-pink-rock-was-found-in-the-sahara-desert-nasa-funded-researchers-have-now-confirmed-it-came-from-mars-more-than-4-1-billion-years-ago-and-preserves-signs-of-the-planets-ancient-water/articleshow/135396990.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-31T22:04:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135397162,imgsize-741262.cms"/></item></channel></rss>